"""Shared-card runner; see docs/card-run.md. Fake transport never uses SSH.

Turn-row protocol: before a multi-job benchmark window, append a ledger row with
event=queued, project=<selected project>, a unique jobId beginning claude-turn-, cores=[],
timingValid=true, and queuedTime as an ISO-8601 timestamp with timezone. While
live (age under three hours), that row keeps our benchmark turn ahead of foreign
queues with later queuedTime values. Running jobs must still drain. Close the
window by appending event=finish with the same jobId and project; ordinary
round-robin yielding then resumes. A later turn row cannot jump an older queue.
"""
